  ### what the two identities above rest on
  The host identity number - numbers_parsed = empty holds whatever the
  kinds are, so on its own it does NOT say that every Number cell with
  a value parsed: the same arithmetic would come out if some valueless
  cells were of another kind and as many Number values had failed to
  parse. Both independent checks of this phase made that point. The
  premise is measurable, so it is measured here, by kind:
    empty cells of kind Number (t absent or t="n"): 5410
    empty cells of every other kind:                 0
  every cell holding neither a value nor a formula is a Number cell: as-expected
  and they are the whole of the empty count: as-expected
  With empty_other = 0 the shortfall number - numbers_parsed is the
  valueless Number cells and nothing else, so no Number value failed
  to parse: 1305578 of 1310988 parsed.

  The resolved identity rests on a second premise. A shared-string cell
  with NO value resolves to Ok(None), a success, so the tool counts it
  resolved without an item being read; independent check 2 of this
  phase built such a package. resolved == shared therefore means every
  shared cell resolved TO AN ITEM only where no such cell exists:
    shared-string cells with no value at all: 0
  no shared-string cell in the corpus is without a value: as-expected

